==Trivia==
*In Japan, and by extension [[Nyanko Daisensou|Nyanko Daisensou]], this Fighter is instead known as [[Vega (Uber Rare Cat)|Vega]], while Bison's name was originally assigned to [[Balrog (Uber Rare Cat)|Balrog]].
** This was likely done proactively when localizing Street Fighter II to avoid legal trouble from real life boxer Mike Tyson's legal team, while perhaps also stemming from the localizers not seeing Bison's original name (Vega) as threatening enough to western players.
*** The title "Boxer" ([[Balrog (Uber Rare Cat)|Balrog]]), "Claw" ([[Vega (Uber Rare Cat)|Vega]]) and "Dictator" (M. Bison) have been adopted to not cause confusion when referring to these three Shadaloo leaders between Japanese and international players.

